# Go Structure & Naming

Follow Effective Go and the Go Code Review Comments. Prefer clarity over cleverness.

## Package & File Layout

- One package per directory; package name is a short, lowercase singular noun (`flag`, `store`, `cache`) — not `utils`, `common`, or `helpers`.
- Directory name matches the package name.
- Split files by responsibility within a package, not by type alone:
  - `handler.go`, `service.go`, `store.go`, `models.go`, `errors.go`
  - `*_test.go` beside the code under test
- Keep `main` thin: put business logic in importable packages under `internal/` or `pkg/`.
- Typical service layout:

```text
cmd/<service>/main.go
internal/<domain>/
  handler.go
  service.go
  store.go
  models.go
```

- Avoid deep nesting; prefer flat packages with clear names.
- Do not put multiple unrelated packages in one directory.

## Naming: Functions & Methods

- MixedCaps / mixedCaps only — never `snake_case` or `kebab-case`.
- Exported: `CreateFlag`, `EvaluateForUser`. Unexported: `loadFromCache`, `parseID`.
- Getters omit `Get`: prefer `Flag()` / `Name()`, not `GetFlag()` / `GetName()`. Exception: when needed to avoid a keyword or clash.
- Prefer verbs for functions that do work: `Create`, `Enable`, `Evaluate`.
- Receiver names are short (1–2 letters from the type): `func (s *Store)`, `func (h *Handler)` — not `this`, `self`, or the full type name.
- Interface names: single-method interfaces often end in `-er` (`Evaluator`, `Storer`). Keep interfaces small and consumer-defined when practical.

```go
// ❌ BAD
func get_user_flag(userId string) {}
func (this *FlagService) GetName() string {}

// ✅ GOOD
func userFlag(userID string) {}
func (s *FlagService) Name() string {}
```

## Naming: Variables & Constants

- Short names for short scopes (`i`, `ctx`, `err`, `ok`); descriptive names for wider scopes.
- Acronyms stay consistent case: `userID`, `HTTPClient`, `APIKey` — not `userId`, `HttpClient`.
- Avoid stuttering with the package: `flag.New()` not `flag.NewFlag()`; `flag.Error` not `flag.FlagError` when clear.
- Error variables: `ErrNotFound`, `errInvalidName`.
- Constants: `MaxRetries`, `DefaultTTL` (exported MixedCaps; unexported mixedCaps). Prefer typed constants over bare magic numbers.

```go
// ❌ BAD
var User_Id string
const max_retries = 3
err := errors.New("not found") // unclear reuse

// ✅ GOOD
var userID string
const maxRetries = 3
var ErrNotFound = errors.New("not found")
```

## Quick Checks

- Exported identifiers need doc comments starting with the name.
- `ctx context.Context` is the first parameter when present.
- `error` is the last return value when present.
